\n- DN500, 1 & 2: 25.2, 40.32, 6300, 7875, 250\n- DN600, 1: 78.75, 126, 6300, 7875, 80\n- DN600, 2: 39.375, 63, 6300, 7875, 160\n- DN700, 1: 200, 320, 10000, 12500, 50\n- DN700, 2: 100, 160, 10000, 12500, 100\n- DN750, 1: 200, 320, 10000, 12500, 50\n- DN750, 2: 100, 160, 10000, 12500, 100\n- DN800, 1: 200, 320, 10000, 12500, 50\n- DN800, 2: 100, 160, 10000, 12500, 100\n- DN900, 2: 158.7, 254, 10000, 12500, 63\n- DN1000, 2: 160, 250, 16000, 20000, 100\n- DN1050, 2: 160, 250, 16000, 20000, 100\n- DN1100, 2: 254, 406.3, 16000, 20000, 63\n- DN1200, 2: 254, 406.3, 16000, 20000, 63\n- DN1350, 2: 400, 640, 16000, 20000, 40\n- DN1400, 2: 400, 640, 16000, 20000, 40\n- DN1500, 2: 400, 640, 16000, 20000, 40\n- DN1600, 2: 400, 640, 16000, 20000, 40\n- DN1650, 2: 400, 640, 16000, 20000, 40\n\nTables 9–12 indicating device:\n\nTable 9 (reduced bore, AC):\n- DN40, DN50, DN65: max 9999999, min 99999, VSI 0.0001\n- DN80: 9999999, 999999, 0.0001\n- DN100, DN125, DN150, DN200: 9999999, 999999, 0.001\n- DN250: 9999999, 9999999, 0.001\n- DN300, DN350, DN400, DN450, DN500, DN600: 9999999, 9999999, 0.01\n\nTable 10 (reduced bore, battery):\n- DN40, DN50: 9999999, 99999, 0.0001\n- DN65: 9999999, 99999, 0.001\n- DN80, DN100, DN125, DN150: 9999999, 999999, 0.001\n- DN200: 9999999, 999999, 0.01\n- DN250, DN300, DN350, DN400, DN450: 9999999, 9999999, 0.01\n- DN500, DN600: 9999999, 9999999, 0.1\n\nTable 11 (full bore, AC):\n- DN40, DN50: 9999999, 99999, 0.0001\n- DN65: 9999999, 999999, 0.0001\n- DN80, DN100, DN125, DN150: 9999999, 999999, 0.001\n- DN200, DN250, DN300: 9999999, 9999999, 0.01\n\nPage 12 continuation (this belongs to Table 11, full bore AC powered, continuing from page 11):\n- DN350, DN400, DN450, DN500, DN600: 9999999, 9999999, 0.1\n- DN700, DN750, DN800, DN900, DN1000, DN1050, DN1100, DN1200: 99999999, 99999999, 0.1\n- DN1350, DN1400, DN1500, DN1600, DN1650, DN1800: 999999999, 99999999, 1\n\nYes, that un-headed table on page 12 top is the continuation of Table 11 (full bore AC). I'll merge it into Table 11's matrix table.\n\nTable 12 (full bore, battery):\n- DN40, DN50: 9999999, 99999, 0.001\n- DN65, DN80, DN100, DN125: 9999999, 999999, 0.001\n- DN150: 9999999, 999999, 0.01\n- DN200, DN250, DN300, DN350, DN400, DN450, DN500: 9999999, 9999999, 0.01\n- DN600: 99999999, 9999999, 0.1\n- DN700, DN750, DN800: 99999999, 99999999, 0.1\n- DN900, DN1000, DN1050, DN1100, DN1200, DN1350, DN1400, DN1500, DN1600, DN1650: 999999999, 99999999, 1\n\nNote Table 12 has no DN1800 (correct per source).\n\nFor indicating device tables, meter sizes are lists like \"DN40, DN50, DN65\". I'll keep meter_sizes as string.\n\nSoftware tables:\n\nTable 3 (FEW41Y.Z & FEW43Y.Z):\nPart code 3KXF208402U0113 (Full functionality):\n- 03.00.03, B26AFE6B, -\n- 03.00.04, 6E98963A, -\n- 03.02.00, E12E5C04, -\n- 03.03.02, D4D1E40B, \"HMI display bug fixes. Low flow output bug fix.\"\n- 03.03.03, CEEF45F1, \"Modbus communication bug fix.\"\n- 03.03.06, DAC51328, -\n- 03.04.00, 277BA336, -\n- 03.04.02, 66624063, -\nPart code 3KXF208402U0313 (Sensus / Logger / Pressure / VKL sensor updater):\n- 02.00.02, 84EBD1C8, -\n- 02.00.04, 5D2D2DDD, -\nPart code 3KXF208402U0513 (Modbus / Pressure / VKL sensor updater):\n- 02.00.01, C28EAA16, -\n- 02.00.05, F517559F, -\n\nTable 4 (FEW45Y.Z) footnote [1]:\nMeasurement (Measurement MCU):\n- 01.02.00, 94E6FAE9\n- 01.03.00, A6C913AF\n- 01.03.01, 2BB4AE79\n4G (Communication MCU):\n- 01.02.00, AE3D9862\n- 01.03.00, 3B33D2C8\n- 01.03.01, FDE7CBB6\n- 01.03.02, CD0C1881\nNB-IoT (Communication MCU):\n- 01.03.00, E5742163\n- 01.03.01, EC4FF9C6\n- 01.03.02, C8CABC2D\n- 01.03.03, 31459473\n\nColumns: communication_or_mcu_part, mcu, software_version, crc_checksum, remarks.\n\nNow matrix_tables structure per schema: {name, columns[], rows[] (object per row), description, footnotes[]}. The R137 example also shows column_units. I'll include column_units where relevant.\n\nFlow tables columns: [\"meter_size\", \"accuracy_class\", \"q1_minimum\", \"q2_transitional\", \"q3_permanent\", \"q4_overload\", \"ratio_q3_q1\"], column_units: [null, null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null].\n\nIndicating device columns: [\"meter_sizes\", \"indicating_range_max\", \"indicating_range_min\", \"verification_scale_interval_max\"], units [null, \"m³\", \"m³\", \"m³\"].\n\nSoftware tables columns: [\"software_part_code\", \"software_part_description\", \"software_version\", \"crc_checksum\", \"remarks\"].\n\nFor Table 4: [\"software_category\", \"mcu\", \"software_version\", \"crc_checksum\", \"remarks\"].\n\nFootnotes in matrix_tables: Table 4 footnote [1]. Also flow tables have the \"Please note...\" conditions — I'll put in description.\n\ncertificate fields:\n- number: \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\" (drop \"revision 12\"? The number field: \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01 revision 12\". I'll put number: \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\", and revision_history captures revision 12. Maybe include revision in number? Better keep canonical number and add \"revision\": not in schema. There's no revision field in certificate schema. I could append \" (revision 12)\". Hmm. The revision_history documents it. I'll set number \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\" and maybe add \"revision\": \"12\"? Not in schema — rule 8 says omit fields not present... but extra fields? The schema defines the shape; adding a non-schema field may be tolerated but risky. I'll include number as \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\" and rely on revision_history. Actually to be safe and informative, I could make number \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01 revision 12\" — no, keep clean. I'll keep just the base number. Hmm, but the revision is important. revision_history has entry revision \"12\" date \"2025-04-07\". That conveys it.\n\n- scheme: \"A\"\n- project_number: \"3903947\"\n- page_total: 13\n- member_state: \"The Netherlands\"\n- date_issued: \"2025-04-07\" (7 April 2025). Format? Not specified; I'll use ISO \"2025-04-07\". Test report dates — also convert to ISO? The schema just says date. I'll use ISO for consistency: \"2020-08-14\" etc.\n- oiml_issuer_id: \"NL1\"\n\nissuing_authority:\n- name: \"NMi Certin B.V.\"\n- address_lines: [\"Thijsseweg 11\", \"2629 JA Delft\", \"The Netherlands\"]\n- person_responsible: \"M.Ph.D. Schmidt\"\n- person_title: null / omit. \"Person responsible: M.Ph.D. Schmidt\" — title unknown; omit.\n- phone: \"+31 88 636 2332\"\n- email: \"certin@nmi.nl\"\n- website: \"www.nmi.nl\"\n- oiml_issuer_id: \"NL1\"\n\napplicants: [{name: \"ABB Limited\", address_lines: [\"Oldends Lane\", \"GL10 3TA Stonehouse\", \"United Kingdom\"]}]\n\nmanufacturers: production locations:\n- ABB Limited (UK) — applicant/manufacturer\n- ABB Engineering (Shanghai) Ltd., [\"No. 4528, Kangxin Highway\", \"Pudong New District, Shanghai\", \"201319\", \"P.R. China\"]\n- ABB Inc., [\"125 E. County Line Road\", \"Warminster, PA 18974\", \"United States of America (USA)\"]\n- ABB India Limited, [\"Plot No. 5 & 6, 2nd Phase, Peenya Industrial Area\", \"Bengaluru – 560058\", \"Karnataka\", \"India\"]\n\ncertified_type:\n- category: \"Water meter\"\n- type_designations: [\"AquaMaster4 FEW4XY.Z\", \"AquaMaster4 FET4\", \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"FEW43Y.Z\", \"FEW45Y.Z\"]. Hmm the \"FET4 *\". The type line: \"Type: AquaMaster4 FEW4XY.Z and FET4 *\". So designations: \"AquaMaster4 FEW4XY.Z\" and \"FET4\". I'll include [\"AquaMaster4 FEW4XY.Z\", \"FET4\"]. Plus the concrete transmitter types mentioned in tables: FEW41Y.Z, FEW43Y.Z, FEW45Y.Z — \"all type/model identifiers mentioned\" per schema, so include them.\n- module_designation: null (not mentioned)\n- description: \"Electromagnetic water meter. X = 1 (standard), 3 (advanced) or 5 (premium, mobile comms - MC) variant; Y = 1, 2, 8 or 9 (integral/remote version, optionally sensor only); Z = R (reduced bore), V (virtual full bore) or F (full bore).\"\n\nmodel_family:\n- family_name: \"AquaMaster4\"\n- models: \n  - {model_id: \"FEW41Y.Z\", label: \"AquaMaster4 standard transmitter\", attributes: {x_code: \"1\", x_variant: \"standard\"}}\n  - {model_id: \"FEW43Y.Z\", label: \"AquaMaster4 advanced transmitter\", attributes: {x_code: \"3\", x_variant: \"advanced\"}}\n  - {model_id: \"FEW45Y.Z\", label: \"AquaMaster4 premium transmitter (mobile comms - MC)\", attributes: {x_code: \"5\", x_variant: \"premium (mobile Comms - MC)\"}}\n  - {model_id: \"FET4\", label: \"AquaMaster4 flow sensor\", attributes: {z_options: \"R (reduced bore), V (virtual full bore), F (full bore)\", y_options: \"1, 2, 8, 9 (integral/remote, optionally sensor only)\"}}\n\ncomponents:\n- {role: \"flow sensor (measuring sensor)\", type_designations: [\"FET4\"], alternatives: null, characteristics: {}}\n- {role: \"flow transmitter (calculating and indicating device)\", type_designations: [\"FEW41Y.Z\", \"FEW43Y.Z\", \"FEW45Y.Z\"], alternatives: \"OR\"}\n\nThe schema components: role, type_designations[], alternatives, characteristics{}. I'll include minimal.\n\ncharacteristics.type_level as discussed.\n\ncharacteristics.config_level: as discussed.\n\nrecommendation: {id: \"R49-1\", edition: 2013, amendment: null, scheme: \"A\", accuracy_classes: [\"1\", \"2\"]}. Edition as int 2013. Hmm \"edition (int)\". Yes 2013. Wait — should id be \"R49\"? The canonicalization example converts \"OIML R 60\" to \"R60\". \"R 49-1 (2013)\" → \"R49-1\". I'll use \"R49-1\". Accuracy classes 1 and 2 → [\"1\", \"2\"].\n\ntest_reports: 7 reports with role \"type_evaluation_report\" (they're the OIML Type Evaluation Report(s)? The cert says \"represented by the sample(s) identified in the OIML Type Evaluation Report\" and \"associated OIML Type Evaluation Report(s)\". The listed reports are the associated reports containing tests and examinations. Role: \"type_evaluation_report\" seems right.) Plus documentation file T11851-9 role \"documentation_file\".\n\nrevision_history: revision strings: \"initial\", \"1\"..\"12\". Dates ISO.\n\nfootnotes:\n- {marker: \"*\", text: \"With X being 1 for standard or 3 for advanced or 5 for premium (mobile Comms - MC) variant; Y being 1, 2, 8 or 9 (integral/remote version, optionally sensor only); Z being R (reduced bore), V (virtual full bore) or F (full bore).\"}\n- {marker: \"1)\", text: \"The software version and checksum are displayed on the meter during the circular sequence every 10 minutes. The software version and checksum are displayed sequentially with first for the Measurement part then the Communications part.\"}\n\nNow the model_level — I decided to rely on matrix tables. But wait, maybe I should include at least model_level for transmitter types with attributes that vary, like EMC and battery. But I already have config_level with axis \"transmitter_type\". That covers it. I'll leave model_level empty/omitted. Hmm, the schema shows model_level[] as part of characteristics; omitting is fine per rule 8.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: should the \"models\" be the DN sizes? The matrix rows are (size, class). The certificate covers a family \"of instruments\" per Tables 5–8. The model_id naming convention could be like \"DN40-AC-reduced\". Too many. I'll keep transmitter-variant models. That's defensible.\n\nLet me also double-check decimal conversions in tables — European commas: 0,05 → 0.05; 0,08 → 0.08; 31,25 → 31.25; 787,5 → 787.5; 100,8 → 100.8; 0,1008 → 0.1008; 0,025 → 0.025; 0,0625 → 0.0625; 0,39375 → 0.39375; 0,1575 → 0.1575; 15,625 → 15.625; 12,5 → 12.5; 157,5 → 157.5; 317,5 → 317.5; 507,9 → 507.9; 253,9 → 253.9; 406,2 → 406.2; 158,7 → 158.7; 204,8 → 204.8; 406,3 → 406.3; 39,375 → 39.375; 25,2 → 25.2; 40,32 → 40.32; 25,6 → 25.6; 12,8 → 12.8; 20,48 → 20.48; 10,24 → 10.24; 2,52 → 2.52; 4,032 → 4.032; 8,064 → 8.064; 5,04 → 5.04; 0,504 → 0.504; 0,8064 → 0.8064; 0,4032 → 0.4032; 0,126 → 0.126; 0,2016 → 0.2016; 1,008 → 1.008; 0,64 → 0.64; 0,0001 → 0.0001 etc.\n\nTable 7 DN900 class1: 158,7 → 158.7; 253,9 → 253.9. Table 8 DN900: 158.7, 254 (254 not 253.9 — source says 254). OK.\n\nTemperature: -25 °C / +55 °C → {min: -25, max: 55}, °C.\n\nWater temp T50 (+0,1 °C / +50 °C) → range {0.1, 50} °C.\n\nMAP: 1,6 MPa → 1.6 MPa (16 bar).\n\nPower: 95 –240 VAC @ 50/60 Hz → voltage {95, 240} V; frequency {50,60} Hz. Battery 2x 3,6 V → \"2x 3.6 V\"; operating range 2,9 - 3,6 V → {2.9, 3.6} V.\n\nNow, characteristic label names:\n- measuring_principle\n- accuracy_class\n- environmental_class\n- electromagnetic_environment\n- mechanical_class\n- ambient_temperature_range\n- water_temperature_class\n- water_temperature_range\n- maximum_admissible_pressure\n- orientation\n- reverse_flow\n- checking_facility\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_class (config)\n- pressure_loss_class (config)\n- power supply items (config)\n\nType_level values structure: each {value, unit_symbol, unit_id, footnote_markers}. unit_id null.\n\nLet me write JSON now. Keep unit_id: null everywhere (I'm not certain of unitsdb IDs; rule says leave null unless certain — I'll leave null).\n\nFor matrix_tables rows — big but necessary. Let me be careful and complete.\n\nFlow table name conventions:\n1. \"General characteristics of the family of instruments — reduced bore, AC mains powered (Table 5)\"\n2. \"... reduced bore, battery / renewable energy powered (Table 6)\"\n3. \"... full bore, AC mains powered (Table 7)\"\n4. \"... full bore, battery / renewable energy powered (Table 8)\"\n\nIndicating device:\n5. \"General characteristics of the indicating device — reduced bore, AC mains powered (Table 9)\"\n6. \"... reduced bore, battery / renewable energy powered (Table 10)\"\n7. \"... full bore, AC mains powered (Table 11, incl. continuation)\"\n8. \"... full bore, battery / renewable energy powered (Table 12)\"\n\nSoftware:\n9. \"Software identification — AquaMaster4 FEW41Y.Z and FEW43Y.Z (Table 3)\"\n10. \"Software identification — AquaMaster4 FEW45Y.Z (Table 4)\" with footnotes.\n\nDescriptions: For flow tables, include the note about Q1..Q4 freely chosen: \"Values Q3 and ratio Q3/Q1 selected from paragraph 4.1 of OIML R49-1:2013; Q1 and Q2 are minimum values with ratio Q2/Q1 = 1.6; Q3 and Q4 are maximum values with ratio Q4/Q3 = 1.25; ratio Q3/Q1 at least 40.\"\n\nFootnotes per table: the software Table 4 footnote [1].\n\nAlso for Table 3 software table spans pages 4–5; I merge.\n\nNow check accuracy class column values: use strings \"1\", \"2\", \"1 & 2\".\n\nRatio values are integers.\n\nLet me also decide on q1/q2/q3/q4 column names: \"q1_min\", \"q2_transitional\", \"q3_permanent\", \"q4_overload\". The header says \"Minimum Q1\", \"Transitional Q2\", \"Permanent Q3\", \"Overload Q4\". Good.\n\nIndicating range columns: \"indicating_range_max\", \"indicating_range_min\", \"verification_scale_interval_max\".\n\nNow for certificate.number — include revision? I'll write \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\" and rely on revision history. Hmm, actually maybe safest to include the full string as displayed: \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01 revision 12\"? I'll go with the base number; revision history disambiguates. Actually, I think including revision is more faithful. The schema doesn't have revision field. I'll add number: \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\". Fine.\n\ncertificate.scheme: \"A\".\n\nNow characteristics.config_level entries in detail:\n\n1. {\n  \"attribute\": \"electromagnetic_environment\",\n  \"axis\": \"transmitter type / antenna configuration\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"FEW41Y.Z or FEW43Y.Z\", \"value\": \"E2\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []},\n    {\"condition\": \"FEW45Y.Z with external antenna cable\", \"value\": \"E1\", ...},\n    {\"condition\": \"FEW45Y.Z without external antenna cable\", \"value\": \"E2\", ...}\n  ]\n}\n\n2. {\n  \"attribute\": \"flow_profile_sensitivity_class\",\n  \"axis\": \"bore type / meter size\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"default (0 x DN upstream and 0 x DN downstream)\", \"value\": \"U0 and D0\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"full bore sizes DN250 and larger (3 x DN upstream and 0 x DN downstream)\", \"value\": \"U3 and D0\"}\n  ]\n}\n\n3. {\n  \"attribute\": \"pressure_loss_class\",\n  \"axis\": \"bore type / meter size\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"reduced bore, DN40 and DN50\", \"value\": \"Δp 40 (0.40 bar)\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"reduced bore, larger than DN50\", \"value\": \"Δp 63 (0.63 bar)\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"full bore, DN40 and DN50\", \"value\": \"Δp 10 (0.10 bar)\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"full bore, DN65 to DN200\", \"value\": \"Δp 16 (0.16 bar)\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"full bore, DN250 and larger\", \"value\": \"Δp 10 (0.10 bar)\"}\n  ]\n}\n\n4. {\n  \"attribute\": \"power_supply_voltage\",\n  \"axis\": \"power supply option\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"AC mains\", \"value\": {\"min\": 95, \"max\": 240}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"renewable energy power (DC powered)\", \"value\": {\"min\": 6, \"max\": 32}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}\n  ]\n}\n\n5. {\n  \"attribute\": \"power_supply_frequency\",\n  \"axis\": \"power supply option\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"AC mains\", \"value\": {\"min\": 50, \"max\": 60}, \"unit_symbol\": \"Hz\"}\n  ]\n}\n\n6. {\n  \"attribute\": \"replaceable_battery\",\n  \"axis\": \"transmitter type\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"FEW41Y.Z / FEW43Y.Z\", \"value\": \"2x 3.6 V (operating range 2.9 V – 3.6 V)\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"FEW45Y.Z\", \"value\": \"6x 3.6 V (operating range 2.9 V – 3.6 V)\"}\n  ]\n}\n\n7. {\n  \"attribute\": \"battery_backup_with_external_power\",\n  \"axis\": \"transmitter type\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"FEW45Y.Z, AC mains or renewable energy powered\", \"value\": \"includes 4x 3.6 V replaceable batteries\"}\n  ]\n}\n\ntype_level:\n{\n  \"measuring_principle\": {\"value\": \"Electromagnetic\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []},\n  \"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": \"1 and 2\", ...},\n  \"environmental_class\": {\"value\": \"O (installed outdoors)\"},\n  \"electromagnetic_environment\": {\"value\": \"E2\"},\n  \"mechanical_class\": {\"value\": \"M1\"},\n  \"ambient_temperature_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": -25, \"max\": 55}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n  \"water_temperature_class\": {\"value\": \"T50\"},\n  \"water_temperature_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 50}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n  \"maximum_admissible_pressure\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"MPa\"},\n  \"orientation\": {\"value\": \"All positions (horizontal, vertical or diagonal)\"},\n  \"reverse_flow\": {\"value\": \"The sensor is intended to measure reverse flow\"},\n  \"checking_facility\": {\"value\": \"Type P (permanent) automatic checking facility\"}\n}\n\nFootnote_markers: [] — include empty arrays? The schema shows footnote_markers[] as part of structured value. I'll include \"footnote_markers\": [] where none. Or omit for brevity. The strict shape shows it; I'll include always to be consistent. That's a lot of repetition in matrix tables? Matrix table rows are plain numbers (per R137 example), so fine.\n\nNow, model_family attributes: I'll include y/z variant info on models.\n\nNow build the JSON. Watch JSON validity: no trailing commas, proper escaping. Use \"°C\", \"m³/h\", \"Δp\" characters — fine in JSON UTF-8.\n\nLet me also handle \"date_issued\": \"2025-04-07\".\n\nTest reports dates:\n- NMi-2254799-01: 2020-08-14, 235 pages\n- NMi-2254799-03: 2020-09-30, 44\n- NMi-2254799-04: 2020-12-24, 180\n- NMi-2564429-01: 2021-08-02, 26\n- NMi-2496280-01: 2021-08-26, 29\n- NMi-2496280-02: 2021-11-23, 25\n- NMi-2563125-01: 2023-09-22, 94\n\nRevision history:\n- initial: 2020-08-14 \"First issue.\"\n- 1: 2020-09-30 \"Additional evaluation of reduced bore larger sizes up to DN600.\"\n- 2: 2020-12-24 \"Additional evaluation of (virtual) full bore sensor and additional software version\"\n- 3: 2021-08-02 \"Additional evaluation for extending temperature to –25 °C and for E2 class and O class for the flow transmitter. Addition of software version.\"\n- 4: 2021-08-26 \"Addition of full-bore sizes up to DN1200.\"\n- 5: 2021-11-23 \"Addition of full-bore sizes up to DN1800.\"\n- 6: 2022-05-20 \"Addition of accuracy class 1 to DN1800.\"\n- 7: 2022-08-30 \"Software version updates due to addition of microprocessors.\"\n- 8: 2023-07-03 \"Software update\"\n- 9: 2023-09-23 \"Addition of AquaMaster4 FEW45Y.Z Mobile comms variant of calculating and indicating device. Software update\"\n- 10: 2024-02-26 \"Software update and change to U200 wireless module for global use.\"\n- 11: 2025-01-27 \"Software update.\"\n- 12: 2025-04-07 \"Hardware update due to the addition of resistor alternatives.\"\n\nComponents: also the indicating device? I'll include three components: flow sensor, transmitter (calculating and indicating device). Also maybe \"wireless module U200\" mentioned in revision 10 — too tangential, skip.\n\nLet me now also decide about certified_type.description. Combine: \"Electromagnetic water meter, type AquaMaster4. Transmitter types FEW4XY.Z: X = 1 (standard), 3 (advanced) or 5 (premium, mobile Comms - MC); Y = 1, 2, 8 or 9 (integral/remote version, optionally sensor only); Z = R (reduced bore), V (virtual full bore) or F (full bore). Flow sensor type FET4.\"\n\nNow, the schema says model_family include ONLY if cert covers >1 model variant — yes it does.\n\nWrite out the full JSON. Be careful with numbers: 9999999 (int), 0.0001 etc.\n\nOne more consideration: In flow matrix tables, should I add \"footnote_markers\" or notes? The \"Please note\" conditions apply to all flow tables — I'll put in description of each flow table.\n\nAlso column_units for flow: [\"DN\", null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null]. meter_size unit \"DN\" is nominal; I'll use null.\n\nSoftware Table 3 rows with part code column repeated per row:\n- part_code: \"3KXF208402U0113\", part_description: \"Full functionality\", version, crc, remarks.\nRemarks \"-\" → null or \"-\"? Use null for \"-\". Actually keep \"-\" as given? I'll use null (empty). The rule: empty strings are not values. \"-\" is a placeholder; I'll use null.\n\nTable 4 columns: [\"software_category\", \"mcu\", \"software_version\", \"crc_checksum\", \"remarks\"] where mcu = \"Measurement MCU\" / \"Communication MCU\". remarks: \"Software identification for Measurement MCU\" etc. → put in mcu column, remarks null.\n\nRows:\nMeasurement: 01.02.00/94E6FAE9, 01.03.00/A6C913AF, 01.03.01/2BB4AE79 — mcu \"Measurement MCU\"\n4G: 01.02.00/AE3D9862, 01.03.00/3B33D2C8, 01.03.01/FDE7CBB6, 01.03.02/CD0C1881 — \"Communication MCU\"\nNB-IoT: 01.03.00/E5742163, 01.03.01/EC4FF9C6, 01.03.02/C8CABC2D, 01.03.03/31459473 — \"Communication MCU\"\n\nFootnotes for table 4: [\"1) The software version and checksum are displayed on the meter during the circular sequence every 10 minutes. The software version and checksum are displayed sequentially with first for the Measurement part then the Communications part.\"] — put under footnotes of that matrix_table, and also in global footnotes.\n\nNow finalize the JSON structure. Size will be large but acceptable.\n\nFor components characteristics — {} empty. Maybe give flow sensor characteristics: bore options. I'll add attributes: {\"bore_options\": \"R (reduced bore), V (virtual full bore), F (full bore)\"}. Keep light.\n\nAlso manufacturers: include ABB Limited first (applicant & manufacturer), then others as production locations.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nCheck: \"Person responsible: M.Ph.D. Schmidt\" — person_responsible: \"M.Ph.D. Schmidt\".\n\nNow produce final JSON. Ensure numbers like 0.025, 0.1008, 0.39375 written correctly. 12,6 in Table 5 DN600 class1 q1: 12.6 (as printed; note this seems like 12.6 rather than 12.5 — keep as printed). Yes source says 12,6. Keep 12.6.\n\nTable 7 DN900 class 2: q2 128; ratio 125. OK.\n\nTable 8 DN900 class 2: 158.7, 254. OK. DN1100: 254, 406.3. DN1000: 160, 250.\n\nWrite JSON carefully.\n\nFor accuracy_classes in recommendation: [\"1\", \"2\"].\n\nscheme \"A\".\n\nEdition: 2013.\n\nAlso \"amendment\": null — omit or null. I'll omit? Schema lists amendment. I'll set null.\n\nCertificate page_total: 13.\n\noiml_issuer_id: \"NL1\".\n\nLet me write the final answer now. I'll be meticulous with the table rows.\n\nTable 5 rows JSON:\n{\"meter_size\":\"DN40\",\"accuracy_class\":\"1\",\"q1_min\":0.05,\"q2_transitional\":0.08,\"q3_permanent\":25,\"q4_overload\":31.25,\"ratio_q3_q1\":500}\n{\"meter_size\":\"DN40\",\"accuracy_class\":\"2\",\"q1_min\":0.025,\"q2_transitional\":0.04,...,1000}\nDN50 1: 0.08, 0.128, 40, 50, 500\nDN50 2: 0.04, 0.064, 40, 50, 1000\nDN65 1&2: 0.063, 0.1008, 63, 78.75, 1000\nDN80 1&2: 0.1, 0.16, 100, 125, 1000\nDN100 1: 0.32, 0.512, 160, 200, 500\nDN100 2: 0.16, 0.256, 160, 200, 1000\nDN125 1: 0.32, 0.512, 160, 200, 500\nDN125 2: 0.16, 0.256, 160, 200, 1000\nDN150 1&2: 0.4, 0.64, 400, 500, 1000\nDN200 1&2: 0.63, 1.008, 630, 787.5, 1000\nDN250 1: 2, 3.2, 1000, 1250, 500\nDN250 2: 1, 1.6, 1000, 1250, 1000\nDN300 1: 3.2, 5.12, 1600, 2000, 500\nDN300 2: 1.6, 2.56, 1600, 2000, 1000\nDN350 1: 3.2, 5.12, 1600, 2000, 500\nDN350 2: 1.6, 2.56, 1600, 2000, 1000\nDN400 1&2: 5, 8, 2500, 3125, 500\nDN450 1&2: 5, 8, 2500, 3125, 500\nDN500 1: 8, 12.8, 4000, 5000, 500\nDN500 2: 4, 6.4, 4000, 5000, 1000\nDN600 1: 12.6, 20.16, 6300, 7875, 500\nDN600 2: 6.3, 10.08, 6300, 7875, 1000\n\nTable 6 rows as listed above.\n\nTable 7 rows as listed (47 rows). Table 8 rows as listed (39 rows).\n\nIndicating tables: rows with meter_sizes strings.\n\nAlright, compose. This will be long but complete.\n\nAlso double check: Table 9 header row has units [mm], [m³]... meter size in mm. column_units: [\"mm\", \"m³\", \"m³\", \"m³\"].\n\nFlow tables header \"Flow rates [m³/h]\".\n\nI'll include \"description\" for each matrix table briefly.\n\nFinal check on issuing authority person_title — the document just says \"Person responsible: M.Ph.D. Schmidt\". \"Certification Board\" appears — not a title. Omit person_title.\n\nOne more: certificate.date_issued \"2025-04-07\" (signature date 7 April 2025). Good.",
